{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["The reason for <b>\"And this is the work of the Menorah\"</b> — to hint that for all generations it must be of hammered work (מקשה), for this is a disqualifying condition in it. Therefore he first mentioned explicitly the requirement of hammered work, and did not mention in its description that it had branches, knobs, and cups cast (משוקדים). And he mentioned <b>gold</b> because so it will be a commandment for all generations to make it from it, to elevate the house of our Elohim. And he reverted to <b>\"it was of hammered work\"</b> to say that there is no disqualifying condition in it except hammered work, not gold, and certainly not the other ornaments upon it. Thus our Rabbis said in Sifrei (Beha'alotkha 61) and in tractate Menahot (Menahot 28a-b):" "The reason for <b>\"so he made it\"</b> — Moses is the one mentioned, for he applied himself to learning its fashion and made it by command. Thus they said in Sifrei (ibid.): to declare the praise of Moses, that just as the Holy One, blessed be He, said to him, so he made it. And Rashi wrote (Rashi on Numbers 8:4): \"so he made it\" — the one who made it was [Moses]; and a midrashic aggadah (Tanhuma, Beha'alotkha 3): by the hand of the Holy One, blessed be He, it was made by itself."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The reference to Menahot 28 is given without page designation in the Hebrew; the standard folio is 28a–28b."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:03:40.567044262Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}